{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The amount of the freewill offering of your hand that you shall give, as YHWH your Elohim blesses you.</b> The Targum of מסת נדבת ידך is 'his requirement' — as in (Deuteronomy 15:8): כמסת חוסרניה — 'according to his need.' And Scripture says: according to the measure of generosity of heart that is in you, and according to the blessing and wealth that you have, you shall give. Therefore the word תתן ('you shall give') was placed in the middle, between מסת נדבת ידך and כאשר יברכך ה' אלהיך — that is to say, according to your generosity and your wealth you shall bring offerings for peace-offerings and consecrate guests at your table." "<b>And it appears</b> that this is not attached to 'the festival of Shavuot to YHWH your Elohim,' but is a matter in itself. And the same rule applies to the rest of the festivals: a person should give charity and consecrate guests according to his generosity and according to his wealth. But this was revealed here, at the festival of Shavuot, because Pesach has a duration of seven days and Sukkot likewise seven days, but Shavuot being only one day, I might have supposed that its matter is not as weighty as the rest of the festivals. Therefore He informed us of the obligation in it: one must not lighten the commandment of charity, for it is equal to the rest of the festivals and weighty like them, even though it is only one day. And these guests are the Levite and the stranger and the orphan and the widow, and this 'stranger' is meant only of the righteous convert, who is a member of the covenant: just as the Levite is a member of the covenant, so too the stranger is a member of the covenant. And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: four of Mine against four of yours. Four of Mine — the Levite and the stranger and the orphan and the widow; four of yours — your son and your daughter and your manservant and your maidservant. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: if you gladden Mine, I will gladden yours. And this is what it says: ״ושמחת לפני ה' אלהיך אתה ובנך ובתך ועבדך ואמתך והלוי והגר והיתום והאלמנה אשר בקרבך״ — 'And you shall rejoice before YHWH your Elohim: you and your son and your daughter and your manservant and your maidservant and the Levite and the stranger and the orphan and the widow who are in your midst.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:48.803413765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}